# THE WINDOWS BOX'S SCHEDULED TASKS -- the DR floor for the machine that touches money.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. `ops/crontab.manifest` is the VPS's answer to "can this repo still
# reconstitute the desk", and `scripts/check_scheduler_manifest.py` keeps it honest. The box had
# NO equivalent. Measured 2026-09-05 across the whole tree: twenty-five MT5-* tasks are named in
# code, `stall_watch.ps1` heals eight of them by name every ten minutes, and FIVE OF THOSE EIGHT
# HAVE NO INSTALLER ANYWHERE IN THIS REPO -- MT5-Gauntlet, MT5-Shadow, MT5-UniversalGate,
# MT5-QQuantShadow, MT5-ResearchSupervisor. They exist only in one machine's task registry.
#
# Two things follow, and both are live today rather than hypothetical:
#
#   THE CADENCE IS UNVERIFIABLE. The standing requirement is that the gauntlet judges, the clocks
#   advance and certificates mint EVERY HOUR. Nothing in this repo can confirm or deny that the
#   box does it, because nothing here declares when those tasks fire. "It runs hourly" has been
#   an assumption, not a fact, for as long as the tasks have existed.
#
#   A REBUILD LOSES THE RESEARCH LANE. Restore this repo onto a fresh box and the gateway, the
#   deadman, the tape recorders and the dashboard come back -- they have installers. The gauntlet,
#   the forward clocks, the universal gate and the supervisor do not come back at all, and nothing
#   would say so: `stall_watch` would report them missing, which reads identically to a task that
#   is merely disabled.
#
# WHAT THIS FILE IS. One line per task, in the box's own vocabulary, so the tasks can be compared
# to what the machine actually runs and rebuilt when it is replaced. It is a MANIFEST, not an
# installer: `scripts/check_box_tasks.py` reads it and reports drift.
#
# UNDECLARED IS WRITTEN AS UNDECLARED. The tasks below carrying `trigger=UNDECLARED` do so because this
# repo does not know their cadence and nobody here may invent one -- a manifest that guessed
# "hourly" would answer the standing question with a fabrication, and the answer would look exactly
# like a measurement. Reading the real trigger off the box (`Get-ScheduledTask -TaskName <name> |
# Select -Expand Triggers`) and pasting it here is a five-minute job that turns five guesses into
# facts, and until it is done this file says exactly which ones remain guesses.
#
# WRITING THIS FILE FOUND THREE INSTALLERS NOBODY HAD LINKED and one task nobody had listed:
# install_moat_miner_task.ps1, install_contract_terms_task.ps1 and install_cachewarm_task.ps1
# carry real triggers, and MT5-MoatFence is named as the tape recorder's watchdog with no
# installer anywhere. That is the manifest earning its place before its fence had even run twice.
#
# FORMAT: one `TASK` line per task, whitespace-separated key="value" pairs.
#   name      the Windows task name, exactly as `stall_watch.ps1` heals it
#   trigger   the repetition, in plain words, or UNDECLARED
#   runs      the script or module it executes, repo-relative where one exists
#   installer the file in THIS repo that registers it, or NONE
#   lane      money | research | data | ops -- what a failure of it costs

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- money path (never research)
# THE ORGANS ADDED 2026-09-12. Each was built, correct, and running nowhere -- the class the
# principal asked to end. MT5-CostState carries the two cost producers that
# check_enforcement_execution measured MENTIONED: each has a main() and writes an
# artifact, and neither had ever been scheduled, so the desk went on charging one flat
# spread per symbol at every hour and zero overnight financing.
TASK name="MT5-MoatCapture"        trigger="every 30 minutes"     runs="desks/mt5/moat/capture_watch.py"        installer="NONE" lane="ops"
TASK name="MT5-ShiftWatch"         trigger="hourly"              runs="desks/mt5/research/shift_watch.py"      installer="NONE" lane="research"
TASK name="MT5-CostState"          trigger="daily 04:20"         runs="desks/mt5/research/cost_surface.py"     installer="NONE" lane="research"
TASK name="MT5-CostState"          trigger="daily 04:20"         runs="desks/mt5/research/carry_state.py"      installer="NONE" lane="research"
TASK name="MT5-CostState"          trigger="daily 04:20"         runs="desks/mt5/research/cost_honesty.py"     installer="NONE" lane="research"
# THE FRONTIER MEASUREMENT LANE. Six organs, one task, daily -- each built, correct and with no
# caller anywhere in this tree until 2026-09-12. certificate_hygiene runs first because it is the
# only one that mutates anything; the rest read the registry it leaves behind.
TASK name="MT5-FrontierAudit"      trigger="daily 05:10"         runs="ops/run_frontier_audit.cmd"            installer="NONE" lane="research"
TASK name="MT5-AuditLane"          trigger="every 1 hour"        runs="ops/run_audit_lane.cmd"                installer="NONE" lane="research"
TASK name="MT5-ScientistTournament" trigger="daily 02:30 local (00:30 UTC)" runs="ops/run_scientist_tournament.cmd" installer="NONE" lane="research"
TASK name="MT5-Gateway"            trigger="continuous loop"      runs="desks/mt5/research/run_gateway_loop.py" installer="NONE" lane="money"
TASK name="MT5-FusionDeadman"      trigger="UNDECLARED"           runs="scripts/run_deadman_switch.py"         installer="NONE" lane="money"
# THE MT5 RAIL, DRY-RUN ONLY (2026-09-08). A separate task from MT5-FusionDeadman above, which runs
# the Tier-3 crypto rail and is not touched. This one evaluates the live MT5 account's rails every
# five minutes and writes data/fusion_deadman_state.json saying what it WOULD do; it arms nothing
# (no `--live`), so its failure costs a measurement, which is why the lane is ops. Arming is the
# principal's decision.
TASK name="MT5-FusionDeadmanDryRun" trigger="every 5 minutes"     runs="desks/mt5/proposals/fusion_deadman.py"  installer="desks/mt5/scripts/Install-QuantWindows.ps1" lane="ops"
TASK name="MT5-TerminalBoot"       trigger="at startup"           runs="terminal64.exe"                        installer="NONE" lane="money"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- the research lane
# THE FIVE THAT `stall_watch` HEALS AND NOTHING HERE INSTALLS. Whether they run hourly -- the
# standing requirement -- cannot be answered from this repo until these five triggers are read off
# the box and written down.
# MT5-Gauntlet now runs through RunGauntlet.cmd, which exports the worker count, memory budget and
# headroom ceiling that `research/judging_throughput.py` measured off THIS box into the environment
# the SEALED external_gauntlet.py already reads. The sealed file is never edited; the cadence below
# is raised to :05 by `judging_throughput.apply_cadence` while the queue is deep and headroom
# exists, and the manifest records the base trigger.
TASK name="MT5-Gauntlet"           trigger="every 10 minutes, at :01 (raised to every 5 by judging_throughput while the queue is deep)" runs="desks/mt5/scripts/RunGauntlet.cmd"      installer="NONE" lane="research"
TASK name="MT5-Shadow"             trigger="every 1 hour, at :55" runs="desks/mt5/research/shadow_cycle.py"          installer="NONE" lane="research"
TASK name="MT5-UniversalGate"      trigger="every 1 hour, at :07" runs="desks/mt5/research/universal_gate.py"        installer="NONE" lane="research"
TASK name="MT5-QQuantShadow"       trigger="every 30 minutes, at :25" runs="desks/mt5/research/qquant_shadow.py"         installer="NONE" lane="research"
TASK name="MT5-ResearchSupervisor" trigger="every 30 minutes, at :26" runs="desks/mt5/research/research_supervisor.py"   installer="NONE" lane="research"
TASK name="MT5-QQuantGatesCertify" trigger="every 1 hour, at :27" runs="desks/mt5/research/qquant_gates.py"          installer="NONE" lane="research"

# Declared here because their installers are in the repo and were read to write these lines.
TASK name="MT5-Hourly"             trigger="every 1 hour (keep-alive of the 24/7 discovery resident)" runs="desks/mt5/research/department_resident.py" installer="desks/mt5/scripts/MT5Hourly.cmd" lane="research"
# THE MOAT SWARMS (M19, principal 2026-09-17): EXPLOIT / EXPLORE / RESURRECT run 100% concurrently
# as 24/7 residents (moat_swarms.py --swarm <name>: singleton lock, engines as children under
# budgets by measured generator yield with floors, discovery_compiler last). Unlimited limit,
# IgnoreNew, SYSTEM; the trigger is a keep-alive.
TASK name="MT5-Moat-Exploit" trigger="at startup + every 10 minutes (keep-alive of a 24/7 resident)" runs="desks/mt5/research/moat_swarms.py" installer="NONE" lane="research"
TASK name="MT5-Moat-Explore" trigger="at startup + every 10 minutes (keep-alive of a 24/7 resident)" runs="desks/mt5/research/moat_swarms.py" installer="NONE" lane="research"
TASK name="MT5-Moat-Resurrect" trigger="at startup + every 10 minutes (keep-alive of a 24/7 resident)" runs="desks/mt5/research/moat_swarms.py" installer="NONE" lane="research"
# THE REGION DEPARTMENTS (principal 2026-09-17): Japan on its own hourly resident (HOURLY_PLAN=
# dept:japan) and the global research OS over every country lab (dept:regions), both 24/7
# residents of department_resident.py like the other nine.
TASK name="MT5-Dept-Japan" trigger="at startup + every 10 minutes (keep-alive of a 24/7 resident)" runs="desks/mt5/research/department_resident.py" installer="NONE" lane="research"
TASK name="MT5-Dept-Regions" trigger="at startup + every 10 minutes (keep-alive of a 24/7 resident)" runs="desks/mt5/research/department_resident.py" installer="NONE" lane="research"
# THE AI MATHEMATICS RESEARCH CIVILIZATION (principal 2026-09-17 / 2026-09-22): twenty-eight
# mathematical traditions on the world model's residual, one leg (math_lab) on its own 24/7
# resident (HOURLY_PLAN=dept:mathlab), like the other departments.
TASK name="MT5-Dept-Mathlab" trigger="at startup + every 10 minutes (keep-alive of a 24/7 resident)" runs="desks/mt5/research/department_resident.py" installer="NONE" lane="research"
# THE ALLOCATOR'S 24/7 REACTION (principal 2026-09-23: "24/7 and not slow ... trades on instant
# macro news"). The hourly `pf_allocator` leg is the BACKSTOP full solve; this resident watches
# MACRO_VIEW / regime_state / REGIME_ROUTER / sleeve_registry / gateway_state / NET_EDGE and
# fires `pf_allocator --mode fast` the moment one of them carries a real state change, then
# publishes the event-to-allocation latency per trigger kind in reports/ALLOCATOR_REACTION.json.
# NOT YET REGISTERED ON THE BOX -- declared here first, as the manifest's own rule requires, so
# `scripts/check_box_tasks.py` reports it as drift until the task exists rather than the task
# existing with nothing declaring it. lane=money: it is the sizing path.
TASK name="MT5-AllocatorPulse" trigger="at startup + every 5 minutes (keep-alive of a 24/7 resident)" runs="desks/mt5/research/allocator_trigger.py" installer="NONE" lane="money"
# THE FOREST FEDERATION (principal 2026-09-17). Eleven regional research civilizations,
# each a 24/7 resident running the eleven agent roles of libs/research/forests.ROLES in
# parallel through desks/mt5/research/forest_runner.py. Japan and global macro already
# have residents (MT5-Dept-Japan, MT5-Dept-Macro) and the four global-LAYER forests ride
# MT5-Dept-Regions, so those six are deliberately NOT repeated here.
TASK name="MT5-Forest-Korea" trigger="at startup + every 10 minutes (keep-alive of a 24/7 resident)" runs="desks/mt5/research/department_resident.py" installer="NONE" lane="research"
TASK name="MT5-Forest-China" trigger="at startup + every 10 minutes (keep-alive of a 24/7 resident)" runs="desks/mt5/research/department_resident.py" installer="NONE" lane="research"
TASK name="MT5-Forest-RussiaCis" trigger="at startup + every 10 minutes (keep-alive of a 24/7 resident)" runs="desks/mt5/research/department_resident.py" installer="NONE" lane="research"
TASK name="MT5-Forest-SouthAsia" trigger="at startup + every 10 minutes (keep-alive of a 24/7 resident)" runs="desks/mt5/research/department_resident.py" installer="NONE" lane="research"
TASK name="MT5-Forest-Asean" trigger="at startup + every 10 minutes (keep-alive of a 24/7 resident)" runs="desks/mt5/research/department_resident.py" installer="NONE" lane="research"
TASK name="MT5-Forest-Oceania" trigger="at startup + every 10 minutes (keep-alive of a 24/7 resident)" runs="desks/mt5/research/department_resident.py" installer="NONE" lane="research"
TASK name="MT5-Forest-Europe" trigger="at startup + every 10 minutes (keep-alive of a 24/7 resident)" runs="desks/mt5/research/department_resident.py" installer="NONE" lane="research"
TASK name="MT5-Forest-NorthAmerica" trigger="at startup + every 10 minutes (keep-alive of a 24/7 resident)" runs="desks/mt5/research/department_resident.py" installer="NONE" lane="research"
TASK name="MT5-Forest-Latam" trigger="at startup + every 10 minutes (keep-alive of a 24/7 resident)" runs="desks/mt5/research/department_resident.py" installer="NONE" lane="research"
TASK name="MT5-Forest-Mena" trigger="at startup + every 10 minutes (keep-alive of a 24/7 resident)" runs="desks/mt5/research/department_resident.py" installer="NONE" lane="research"
TASK name="MT5-Forest-Africa" trigger="at startup + every 10 minutes (keep-alive of a 24/7 resident)" runs="desks/mt5/research/department_resident.py" installer="NONE" lane="research"
TASK name="MT5-Deepening"          trigger="every 1 hour"  runs="desks/mt5/research/deepening_worker.py"  installer="desks/mt5/scripts/install_deepening_task.ps1" lane="research"

